versifying into digital assets. This isn’t just another corporate investment—it represents a calculated move by a publicly traded company to position itself in the evolving digital economy. The ZEC cryptocurrency acquisition shows that institutional players see long-term value in privacy-enhancing blockchain technologies. Why Are Companies Investing in ZEC Cryptocurrency? Several factors make ZEC cryptocurrency attractive to institutional investors like Leap Therapeutics: Privacy features that offer transactional confidentiality Proven technology with a established track record Regulatory clarity compared to newer digital assets Portfolio diversification beyond traditional assets Long-term growth potential in the privacy coin sector The ZEC cryptocurrency market has shown resilience despite broader market fluctuations, making it an appealing option for corporate treasury management. Moreover, the transparent nature of blockchain allows investors and regulators to verify holdings while maintaining transaction privacy. How Does This Impact the Broader ZEC Cryptocurrency Market? When publicly traded companies make substantial ZEC cryptocurrency purchases, it creates positive ripple effects throughout the ecosystem. Institutional validation often leads to increased mainstream acceptance and can influence other corporations to consider similar moves. This latest ZEC cryptocurrency investment by Leap Therapeutics follows a growing trend of companies allocating portions of their treasury to digital assets. However, it’s important to note that such investments come with both opportunities and challenges that require careful consideration. What Challenges Do Companies Face with ZEC Cryptocurrency Investments? While the potential rewards are significant, institutional ZEC cryptocurrency investments present several considerations: Regulatory compliance requirements Secure storage solutions for digital assets Price volatility management Shareholder and stakeholder communication Accounting and reporting standards Despite these challenges, the growing number of companies entering the ZEC cryptocurrency space suggests that the benefits often outweigh the risks for well-prepared organizations. What’s Next for Institutional ZEC Cryptocurrency Adoption? The continued expansion of Leap Therapeutics’ ZEC cryptocurrency position indicates that we’re likely to see more companies follow suit. As regulatory frameworks become clearer and custody solutions more sophisticated, institutional adoption of privacy-focused cryptocurrencies is expected to accelerate. This trend could potentially drive increased liquidity and stability in the ZEC cryptocurrency market, benefiting both institutional and retail investors. The growing corporate interest also validates the underlying technology and use cases for privacy coins in the digital economy. In conclusion, Leap Therapeutics’ substantial ZEC cryptocurrency investment represents more than just a corporate treasury decision—it’s a vote of confidence in the future of privacy-focused digital assets. As companies continue to recognize the strategic value of cryptocurrency diversification, we can expect to see more institutional players entering the space, potentially reshaping how corporations manage their assets in the digital age. Frequently Asked Questions What is ZEC cryptocurrency? ZEC is the native cryptocurrency of Zcash, a privacy-focused blockchain that offers selective transparency features for transactions. Why would a company invest in ZEC cryptocurrency? Companies invest in ZEC for portfolio diversification, exposure to privacy technology, and potential long-term growth in the digital asset space. How much ZEC does Leap Therapeutics now hold? Following this latest purchase, Leap Therapeutics holds 232,644 ZEC tokens total across their investment portfolio. Is institutional investment in cryptocurrency increasing? Yes, more publicly traded companies are allocating portions of their treasury to cryptocurrencies as regulatory clarity improves and custody solutions advance. What makes ZEC different from other cryptocurrencies? ZEC offers enhanced privacy features through zero-knowledge proofs, allowing users to shield transaction details while maintaining blockchain security. Are corporate cryptocurrency investments risky? Like any investment, cryptocurrency carries risks including price volatility and regulatory uncertainty, but many companies manage these through proper risk assessment and security measures. Found this analysis of institutional ZEC cryptocurrency investment valuable? Share this article with your network on social media to spread awareness about growing corporate adoption of digital assets! To learn more about the latest cryptocurrency trends, explore our article on key developments shaping institutional cryptocurrency adoption and future market dynamics. This post Strategic ZEC Cryptocurrency Investment: Leap Therapeutics Buys $18M More in Bold Crypto Move first appeared on BitcoinWorld .', 'KEYWORDS': 'Crypto News|BLOCKCHAIN|CRYPTOCURRENCY|Digital Assets|Institutional Investment|Zcash', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'POSITIVE', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1763476457, 'UPDATED_ON': None, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 82, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'bitcoinworld', 'NAME': 'Bitcoin World', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/82/default.png', 'URL': 'https://bitcoinworld.co.in/feed/', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': None, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 0, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1763476746, 'CREATED_ON': 1698066984, 'UPDATED_ON': 1747932437}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 13, 'NAME': 'BLOCKCHAIN', 'CATEGORY': 'BLOCKCHAIN'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 37, 'NAME': 'MARKET', 'CATEGORY': 'MARKET'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 61, 'NAME': 'ZEC', 'CATEGORY': 'ZEC'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 209, 'NAME': 'DIGITAL ASSET TREASURY', 'CATEGORY': 'DIGITAL ASSET TREASURY'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 211, 'NAME': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY', 'CATEGORY': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 54570938, 'GUID': '6ea57795-709f-4ed5-b49f-403fb4ff9a5a', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1763471362, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/5/54570938.jpeg', 'TITLE': 'Fidelity Introduces FSOL ETF, Bringing Major Wall Street Name to Solana Funds', 'SUBTITLE': 'The firm’s staking-enabled Solana fund debuts as inflows into early SOL products accelerate.', 'AUTHORS': 'Helene Braun', 'URL': 'https://www.coindesk.com/markets/2025/11/18/fidelity-launches-fsol-fund-bringing-major-wall-street-name-to-solana-etfs', 'SOURCE_ID': 5, 'BODY': 'The firm’s staking-enabled Solana fund debuts as inflows into early SOL products accelerate.', 'KEYWORDS': 'Markets|Fidelity|ETFs|Solana News|News', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'POSITIVE', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1763471418, 'UPDATED_ON': 1763471418, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 5, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'coindesk', 'NAME': 'CoinDesk', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/5/default.png', 'URL': 'https://www.coindesk.com/arc/outboundfeeds/rss/?outputType=xml', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': 1367884800, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 71, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1763476830, 'CREATED_ON': 1657730129, 'UPDATED_ON': 1744296800}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 37, 'NAME': 'MARKET', 'CATEGORY': 'MARKET'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 46, 'NAME': 'SOL', 'CATEGORY': 'SOL'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 211, 'NAME': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY', 'CATEGORY': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 54570935, 'GUID': 'https://cryptonews.com/?p=453099', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1763471322, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://images.cryptocompare.com/news/default/cryptonews.png', 'TITLE': 'Bitcoin Price Prediction: 95% of All BTC Just Got Mined – Real Scarcity Starting Now?', 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': 'Arslan Butt', 'URL': 'https://cryptonews.com/news/bitcoin-price-prediction-95-of-all-btc-just-got-mined-real-scarcity-starting-now/', 'SOURCE_ID': 52, 'BODY': 'Bitcoin reached a key supply milestone this week, with total mined coins exceeding 19.95 million BTC, or 95% of its fixed 21 million cap. Fewer than 1.05 million BTC are left to be mined, and issuance will slow sharply as the network advances through future halvings. Permanently Lost and Unspendable BTC A portion of Bitcoin’s supply can never re-enter circulation. Roughly 230 BTC are unspendable due to the genesis block subsidy and early invalid scripts. Additional coins are believed lost through forgotten or unrecoverable private keys, further tightening the effective supply. How Bitcoin’s Halvings Cut Issuance Bitcoin’s supply halves every 210,000 blocks. The most recent halving on April 20, 2024, reduced block rewards from 6.25 BTC to 3.125 BTC, lowering daily issuance from 900 BTC to about 450 BTC. Earlier halvings in 2012, 2016, and 2020 brought the subsidy down from 50 BTC to its current level, pushing annualized supply growth below 1%. The next halving is estimated for April 2028, and the final fractions of Bitcoin are expected to be mined around 2140. Bitcoin (BTC/USD) Price Pullback Aligns With Technical Weakness Despite a tightening supply, price action has weakened. Bitcoin has fallen toward the mid-$80,000s, breaking below a long-term ascending trendline that supported most of the 2024 advance. BTC now trades under both the 20-EMA and 50-EMA on the daily chart, reinforcing bearish momentum. Bitcoin Price Chart – Source: Tradingview The chart also reflects a completed ABCD pattern near the $115,000 high and a breakdown from a rising wedge, both common precursors to broader corrections. Price is approaching the $83,800–$74,500 demand zone, an area that previously generated strong buying interest. RSI near 28 shows oversold conditions, although a clear bullish divergence has not yet formed. TradingView’s projected path suggests BTC may drift slightly lower before forming a stabilization pattern within the demand zone. A hammer or bullish engulfing candle would signal buyer re-entry. Levels to Watch in the Weeks Ahead A recovery above $96,000 would be the first sign of stabilization. A move through $100,700 could open the way to a retest of $115,200, provided sentiment improves. Failure to hold the demand area would expose $74,500 as the next key level. For traders, current conditions resemble the early phase of an accumulation zone. If BTC reclaims its short-term EMAs and confirms support, the next rally could extend to major altcoins, including ETH, SOL, and XRP. Bitcoin Hyper: The Next Evolution of BTC on Solana? Bitcoin Hyper ($HYPER) is bringing a new phase to the Bitcoin ecosystem. While BTC remains the gold standard for security, Bitcoin Hyper adds what it always lacked: Solana-level speed. The result: lightning-fast, low-cost smart contracts, decentralized apps, and even meme coin creation, all secured by Bitcoin. Audited by Consult , the project emphasizes trust and scalability as adoption builds. And momentum is already strong. The presale has surpassed $27 million, with tokens priced at just $0.013265 before the next increase. As Bitcoin activity climbs and demand for efficient BTC-based apps rises, Bitcoin Hyper stands out as the bridge uniting two of crypto’s biggest ecosystems. If Bitcoin built the foundation, Bitcoin Hyper could make it fast, flexible, and fun again. Click Here to Participate in the Presale The post Bitcoin Price Prediction: 95% of All BTC Just Got Mined – Real Scarcity Starting Now? appeared first on Cryptonews .', 'KEYWORDS': 'Price Analysis|Bitcoin|Cryptocurrency', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'NEGATIVE', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1763471355, 'UPDATED_ON': None, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 52, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'cryptonews', 'NAME': 'cryptonews', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://images.cryptocompare.com/n