1367884800, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 71, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1763476830, 'CREATED_ON': 1657730129, 'UPDATED_ON': 1744296800}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 54, 'NAME': 'USDT', 'CATEGORY': 'USDT'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 211, 'NAME': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY', 'CATEGORY': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 54573317, 'GUID': 'https://u.today/103-billion-crypto-crash-peter-brandt-names-one-condition-for-market-reversal', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1763471055, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/64/54573317.jpeg', 'TITLE': '$1.03 Billion Crypto Crash: Peter Brandt Names One Condition for Market Reversal', 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': 'U.Today', 'URL': 'https://u.today/103-billion-crypto-crash-peter-brandt-names-one-condition-for-market-reversal', 'SOURCE_ID': 64, 'BODY': 'Legendary trader Peter Brandt has weighed in on recent market declines, naming one condition under which the bearish price action might be reversed.', 'KEYWORDS': 'Peter Brandt', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'NEUTRAL', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1763477800, 'UPDATED_ON': 1763477801, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 64, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'utoday', 'NAME': 'U.Today', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://images.cryptocompare.com/news/default/utoday.png', 'URL': 'https://u.today/cryptocompare.php', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': 1506816000, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 49, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1763476832, 'CREATED_ON': 1657730129, 'UPDATED_ON': 1745920032}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 37, 'NAME': 'MARKET', 'CATEGORY': 'MARKET'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 50, 'NAME': 'TRADING', 'CATEGORY': 'TRADING'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 54570796, 'GUID': 'https://www.newsbtc.com/?p=854888', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1763470856, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/21/54570796.jpeg', 'TITLE': 'Here’s Why The Bitcoin Price Could Pump To $110,000 This Week', 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': 'Sandra White', 'URL': 'https://www.newsbtc.com/news/bitcoin/bitcoin-price-pump-to-110000/', 'SOURCE_ID': 21, 'BODY': 'The Bitcoin price has spent the past few days struggling to recover from its sharp breakdown below $100,000, a move that rattled traders and briefly pushed the crypto market into one of its weakest phases in many months. Bitcoin’s price action has hovered in the mid-$90,000 range since the drop, but the past 24 hours have been highlighted by a break below $90,000. In the middle of this bearish volatility, a new technical outlook from Tony “The Bull” Severino suggests that Bitcoin’s next move may be more bullish than the recent weakness implies. A Death Cross Forms During The Bitcoin Price Downtrend Tony’s analysis highlights the developing death cross on the daily timeframe, where the 50-day moving average is now bending down toward the 200-day moving average. The pattern is generally viewed as bearish, but the placement of the moving averages and the slope of the short-term line show something different unfolding on Bitcoin’s chart. Related Reading: Here’s Why The Ethereum Price Is Crashing Again, Can It Breach $3,000? The green 50-day average has been gradually drifting lower after weeks of fading momentum, and the red 200-day average has begun flattening out from the long-term uptrend.\\xa0As shown on the chart below, this death cross has formed around $110,000, and according to the analyst, Bitcoin might pump into this price level next week. The reason a pump remains possible at this stage is tied directly to how moving averages behave. After the breakdown beneath $100,000, Bitcoin found support just below $92,000 and has since been forming a series of smaller-bodied candles that reflect the early stages of a potential reversal. If buyers take control, a fast move toward the region between $103,000 and $110,000 becomes realistic. However, price action in the past 24 hours, which has seen Bitcoin break below $90,000, threatens this bullish outlook. Bitcoin Price Chart. Source: @TonyTheBullCMT On X The Path To $110,000 This Week For Bitcoin to reach $110,000 in the coming days, the market would need to replay a pattern seen several times in past cycles: a strong relief rally just before or immediately after a death cross forms. These rallies happen because sentiment becomes overly pessimistic at the exact moment when shorts begin to pile in, leaving the price vulnerable to a sharp upside reaction. However, for that scenario to unfold now, Bitcoin would first need to push convincingly back above $90,000 and show that momentum is shifting away from the recent sell-off. Related Reading: This Analyst Called The Bitcoin Crash Below $20,000 In 2021, He’s Back With A Shocking Prediction For Solana Interestingly, other analysts have pointed to bullish primers for Bitcoin, despite the bearish price action. One such case is the Bitcoin SSR RSI, which was highlighted by a CryptoQuant community analyst called Maartunn, that shows rising stablecoin buying power relative to Bitcoin’s market cap. On the other hand, a bearish indicator has risen up with the SuperTrend indicator, which proposes a further 67% drop in the price of Bitcoin. At the time of writing, Bitcoin is trading at $89,760, down by 5.8% in the past 24 hours. Featured image created with Dall.E, chart from Tradingview.com', 'KEYWORDS': 'Bitcoin|bitcoin|Bitcoin news|bitcoin price|btc|BTC news|btc price|btcusd|BTCUSDT', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'NEUTRAL', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1763470948, 'UPDATED_ON': 1763470948, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 21, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'newsbtc', 'NAME': 'NewsBTC', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://images.cryptocompare.com/news/default/newsbtc.png', 'URL': 'https://www.newsbtc.com/feed/', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': 1380585600, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 50, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1763476831, 'CREATED_ON': 1657730129, 'UPDATED_ON': 1711620962}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 14, 'NAME': 'BTC', 'CATEGORY': 'BTC'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 24, 'NAME': 'ETH', 'CATEGORY': 'ETH'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 37, 'NAME': 'MARKET', 'CATEGORY': 'MARKET'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 50, 'NAME': 'TRADING', 'CATEGORY': 'TRADING'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 211, 'NAME': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY', 'CATEGORY': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 54572404, 'GUID': 'https://ambcrypto.com/?p=546976', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1763470856, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://images.cryptocompare.com/news/default/ambcrypto.png', 'TITLE': 'Crypto winter ahead? 28% market crash & Bitcoin’s price drop sparks panic', 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': 'Akashnath S', 'URL': 'https://ambcrypto.com/crypto-winter-ahead-29-market-crash-bitcoins-price-drop-sparks-panic/', 'SOURCE_ID': 32, 'BODY': 'We are not definitively in a bear market, but winter was certainly advancing on crypto town.', 'KEYWORDS': 'Bitcoin|BTC Trading View|News|News 1|Social|Trading View|ambcrypto', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'NEGATIVE', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1763476187, 'UPDATED_ON': None, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 32, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'ambcrypto', 'NAME': 'AMB Crypto', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://images.cryptocompare.com/news/default/ambcrypto.png', 'URL': 'https://ambcrypto.com/feed/', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': None, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 0, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1763476754, 'CREATED_ON': 1657730129, 'UPDATED_ON': 1674467937}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 14, 'NAME': 'BTC', 'CATEGORY': 'BTC'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 37, 'NAME': 'MARKET', 'CATEGORY': 'MARKET'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 50, 'NAME': 'TRADING', 'CATEGORY': 'TRADING'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 211, 'NAME': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY', 'CATEGORY': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 54572533, 'GUID': 'https://www.cryptopolitan.com/?p=863225', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1763470852, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/43/54572533.jpeg', 'TITLE': 'Lloyds agrees to acquire digital wallet provider Curve for $139M despite investor backlash', 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': 'Florence Muchai', 'URL': 'https://www.cryptopolitan.com/lloyds-acquire-digital-wallet-provider-curve/', 'SOURCE_ID': 43, 'BODY': 'Lloyds Banking Group has agreed to acquire British digital asset wallet service provider Curve in a deal worth £120 million ($139 million), according to people briefed on the transaction speaking to Sky News. According to the latest report from Sky News on the matter, the agreement is set to be announced formally next week. Curve told its shareholders in recent days that it had signed a share sale and purchase contract with Lloyds, which could see the UK’s largest high street bank make its most significant step into digital payments yet. Yet, according to insiders’ understanding, the purchase has sparked a dispute among some of Curve’s top shareholders, who believe the valuation is significantly below what the platform is truly worth. Curve acquisition by UK bank not in the clear yet According to anonymous sources, the company, boasting over six million users, could exhaust its cash reserves this year if a buyer is not secured. In early September, Chief Executive Shachar Bialick admitted that Lloyds Banking Group offered a valuation that was low compared to its previous fundraising rounds, but insisted that Curve needs to secure its future regardless of the sale. Curve has raised more than £250 million ($289 million) since its launch, including a £37 million ($42.8 million) funding round that took place in March this year, led by Hanco Ventures. We see issuers looking to enter the market, and networks introducing innovative products such as Visa Flex and MasterCard One Credentials. This investment would allow us to invest further in our customer experience, bring new partnerships, and accelerate our path to profitability. Shachar Bialick. The current deal values the business at a fraction of those investments, a gap that has been blasted by Curve’s shareholders, now seeking legal means to stop its sale. IDC Ventures threatens Curve and Lloyds Banking Group Sky News reported that Curve’s early shareholders, including IDC Ventures, the company’s largest external investor with a 12% holding, have publicly rejected the deal and are threatening legal action. IDC Ventures issued a statement saying it is deeply worried about how Curve’s management and board handled the sale talks. A company spokesperson told Sky that governance issues and ownership questions were unresolved at the time of the agreement, and argued that the transaction was not in the company’s best interests. It is a matter of real surprise to shareholders that Lloyds Banking Group would contemplate proceeding with a transaction that IDC believes is not in the best interests of the company or its shareholders. IDC does not intend to support the proposed sale and does not believe that it is capable of being implemented without its support. IDC Curve, in its message to shareholders, acknowledged the disappointment around the valuation, adding that the offer failed to meet the expectations set beforehand. We recognise that the value of this transaction falls short of the ambitions we all held for Curve, and we share the disappointment some of you may have in this outcome. Yet, the board strongly believes this transaction represents the best available path forward for Curve’s creditors and shareholders as a whole. Curve. IDC Ventures said last Friday it would defend its commercial interests and asked both Curve and Lloyds to address its concerns before moving ahead with the acquisition . Curve wallet is facing internal leadership and governance issues In July, IDC Ventures attempted to remove Lord Stanley Fink, the former Conservative Party treasurer and a high-profile City figure, from his position as chair of Curve. The fund propounded that the appointing shareholder had already removed him, only for the board to reinstall him two days later. During Curve’s extraordinary general meeting (EGM) in early October, opponents failed to remove both Fink and chief executive Bialick through a shareholder vote. IDC Ventures, represented by the London-based law firm Quinn Emanuel, has been involved with Curve for six years and has participated in several major funding rounds. In a statement shared with Sky News last month, the investor said it was troubled by the reappointment of Fink and by the lack of transparency around the board’s handling of the sale process. Get seen where it counts. Advertise in Cryptopolitan Research and reach crypto’s sharpest investors and builders.', 'KEYWORDS': 'News|BTC|ETH|GBP|Lloyds', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'NEGATIVE', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1763476470, 'UPDATED_ON': 1763478753, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 43, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'cryptopolitan', 'NAME': 'Cryptopolitan', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://images.cryptocompare.com/news/default/cryptopolitan.png', 'URL': 'https://www.cryptopolitan.com/feed/', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': None, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 0, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1763476750, 'CREATED_ON': 1657730129, 'UPDATED_ON': 1681205909}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 14, 'NAME': 'BTC', 'CATEGORY': 'BTC'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 15, 'NAME': 'BUSINESS', 'CATEGORY': 'BUSINESS'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 24, 'NAME': 'ETH', 'CATEGORY': 'ETH'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 41, 'NAME': 'REGULATION', 'CATEGORY': 'REGULATION'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 211, 'NAME': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY', 'CATEGORY': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 54572403, 'GUID': 'https://ambcrypto.com/?p=547165', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1763470834, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://images.cryptocompare.com/news/default/ambcrypto.png', 'TITLE': 'A rare window of opportunity: FUNToken’s deflationary setup', 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': 'AMBCrypto Team', 'URL': 'https://ambcrypto.com/a-rare-window-of-opportunity-funtokens-deflationary-setup/', 'SOURCE_ID': 32, 'BODY': 'Every once in a while, a token enters a phase that long-term investors call a', 'KEYWORDS': 'Fun Token|Google News|HideCryptopanic|Social|SPN News|featured', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'NEUTRAL', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1763476187, 'UPDATED_ON': None, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 32, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'ambcrypto', 'NAME': 'AMB Crypto', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://images.cryptocompare.com/news/default/ambcrypto.png', 'URL': 'https://ambcrypto.com/feed/', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': None, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 0, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1763476754, 'CREATED_ON': 1657730129, 'UPDATED_ON': 1674467937}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 15, 'NAME': 'BUSINESS', 'CATEGORY': 'BUSINESS'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 47, 'NAME': 'SPONSORED', 'CATEGORY': 'SPONSORED'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 54570795, 'GUID': 'https://bitcoinworld.co.in/?p=220341', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1763470814, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/82/default.png', 'TITLE': 'Dollar positioning transforms as investors dramatically slash short positions – BofA reveals shocking shift', 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': 'Jayshree', 'URL': 'https://bitcoinworld.co.in/dollar-positioning-investors-shorts-shift/', 'SOURCE_ID': 82, 'BODY': 'BitcoinWorld Dollar positioning transforms as investors dramatically slash short positions – BofA reveals shocking shift The forex market is witnessing a dramatic transformation in dollar positioning that could signal major changes ahead for currency traders and cryptocurrency investors alike. According to recent Bank of America reports, investors are rapidly reducing their short positions on the US dollar, creating ripple effects across global markets. Understanding the dollar positioning shift Bank of America’s latest analysis reveals significant changes in how institutional investors are approaching the US dollar. The current dollar positioning reflects a notable departure from recent trends, with hedge funds and large speculators scaling back their bearish bets. This shift in dollar positioning comes amid changing expectations about Federal Reserve policy and global economic conditions. Why investors reduce shorts now Several factors are driving why investors reduce shorts at this particular moment. The primary reasons include: Changing interest rate expectations Global economic uncertainty Technical market signals Risk management considerations When investors reduce shorts, it typically indicates a reassessment of market conditions and risk appetite. The current move suggests traders are becoming less confident about dollar weakness in the near term. Key insights from BofA reports The latest BofA reports provide crucial data points for understanding market sentiment. According to their analysis: Metric Previous Position Current Position Change Net Short Positions -$25.6B -$18.3B +$7.3B Long Positions $42.1B $48.9B +$6.8B Short Positions $67.7B $67.2B -$0.5B The BofA reports highlight that this isn’t just a minor adjustment but represents a meaningful change in market positioning. Impact on the broader forex market These positioning changes are creating significant waves throughout the forex market. Major currency pairs are experiencing increased volatility as market participants adjust their strategies. The forex market implications extend beyond just dollar pairs, affecting cross rates and emerging market currencies as well. What the currency outlook suggests The current currency outlook appears to be shifting toward dollar strength, at least in the short term. However, the longer-term currency outlook remains uncertain due to several competing factors: Diverging central bank policies Geopolitical tensions Inflation dynamics Growth differentials Actionable insights for traders For active traders and investors, these developments offer several important considerations. Monitoring dollar positioning changes can provide early signals about market direction. The fact that investors reduce shorts suggests caution may be warranted for those betting on continued dollar weakness. FAQs What does Bank of America track in their currency reports? Bank of America (BofA) monitors futures positions, options activity, and cash market flows to assess market positioning. How often do these positioning reports come out? Major banks including Bank of America typically provide weekly updates on futures positioning and monthly deeper analysis. What other institutions provide similar analysis? Other major financial institutions like Goldman Sachs and JPMorgan Chase also publish regular currency positioning analysis. How reliable are these positioning indicators? While not perfect predictors, positioning data from sources like Bank of America provide valuable context about market sentiment extremes. The dramatic shift in dollar positioning represents a crucial moment for currency markets. As investors reduce shorts and reassess their outlook, the implications could extend far beyond traditional forex trading into cryptocurrency markets and global risk assets. This repositioning suggests markets are entering a new phase where dollar strength may surprise many participants. To learn more about the latest forex market trends, explore our articles on key developments shaping US Dollar positioning and institutional trading strategies. This post Dollar positioning transforms as investors dramatically slash short positions – BofA reveals shocking shift first appeared on BitcoinWorld .', 'KEYWORDS': 'Forex News|#Markets|banking|Dollar|Forex|investing', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'NEUTRAL', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1763470886, 'UPDATED_ON': None, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 82, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'bitcoinworld', 'NAME': 'Bitcoin World', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/82/default.png', 'URL': 'https://bitcoinworld.co.in/feed/', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': None, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 0, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1763476746, 'CREATED_ON': 1698066984, 'UPDATED_ON': 1747932437}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 15, 'NAME': 'BUSINESS', 'CATEGORY': 'BUSINESS'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 26, 'NAME': 'FIAT', 'CATEGORY': 'FIAT'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 37, 'NAME': 'MARKET', 'CATEGORY': 'MARKET'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 50, 'NAME': 'TRADING', 'CATEGORY': 'TRADING'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 210, 'NAME': 'MACROECONOMICS', 'CATEGORY': 'MACROECONOMICS'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 54572531, 'GUID': 'https://www.cryptopolitan.com/?p=863247', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1763470800, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/43/54572531.jpeg', 'TITLE': 'BlockDAG vs Remittix – Which Presale Are Traders Hedging With As The Bitcoin Price Tipped To Sink Further', 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': 'Cryptopolitan Media', 'URL': 'https://www.cryptopolitan.com/blockdag-vs-remittix-which-presale-are-traders-hedging-with-as-the-bitcoin-price-tipped-to-sink-further/', 'SOURCE_ID': 43, 'BODY': 'With the Bitcoin price flirting with a potential downturn, many crypto investors are reconsidering where to allocate fresh capital. As BTC’s momentum weakens, ambitious traders are eyeing BlockDAG and Remittix , two very different presale projects, as hedges or high-growth plays. The fear of missing out (FOMO) is intensifying: is now the moment to lock into long-term altcoin bets? In a market where risk is high, BlockDAG promises next-gen layer-1 infrastructure, while Remittix pitches itself as a cross-border, fiat-crypto payment juggernaut. Both come with their own hype, scarcity, and potential — but which one are traders really leaning into as Bitcoin edges uncertainly? BlockDAG: The High-Scale Layer-1 Gamble BlockDAG has become something of a lightning rod in presale circles. It combines a Directed Acyclic Graph (DAG) structure with Proof-of-Work consensus. According to its team, this hybrid architecture could rival or even outperform traditional cryptos. The presale has already raised hundreds of millions. Reports say over $354 million has been raised. That kind of scale is pushing BlockDAG into “institutional + retail combo” hype territory — and that’s drawing serious trader attention. On top of that, they’ve offered a rare incentive: an “80% unlock” for early backers. But it’s not all sunshine. Some analysts and community members are sounding alarm bells. Critics point out repeated delays and persistent uncertainty around liquidity. Others worry that the presale may be overstaying its welcome, or that the huge amount raised could lead to post-launch sell pressure. Remittix: A PayFi Power Play Remittix plays a completely different game. Rather than chasing blockchain scale, it’s focused on real-world payments: allowing users to convert crypto to fiat and send it directly to bank accounts in 30+ countries. This is not just a speculative altcoin — it’s aiming to be a bridge between crypto and traditional finance. In its presale, Remittix has raised over $28.1 million, selling more than 686 million RTX tokens. That kind of raise, paired with its secured CEX listings on BitMart and LBank, signals traction, not just hype. To top it off, Remittix is fully audited by CertiK, and currently ranks #1 on CertiK Skynet for pre-launch tokens — a major trust signal for risk-sensitive crypto investors. For traders watching Bitcoin wobble, Remittix offers a creative hedge: not just a bet on altcoin appreciation, but a play on crypto adoption in the payments space. Because it’s more than a token — it’s a potential fiat-crypto bridge — many see this as the next big altcoin in 2025 with real-world utility. Why Remittix Is Attracting Hedgeflow Global Reach: Converts crypto to fiat and sends it to bank accounts in 30+ countries. Real-World Utility: It’s built for payments, not just trading — a next-generation DeFi project designed to solve actual financial friction. Multi-Chain Support: Early wallet beta supports Ethereum and Solana, showing cross-chain ambition Security & Trust: Fully audited by CertiK, and ranked #1 for pre-launch safety. Scarcity + Demand: With over $28 million presale and rising demand, early-buyers are already talking about the “XRP 2.0” narrative. Discover the future of PayFi with Remittix by checking out their project here: Website: https://remittix.io Socials: https://linktr.ee/remittix $250, 000 Giveaway: https://gleam.io/competitions/nz84L-250000-remittix-giveaway', 'KEYWORDS': 'Press Release', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'NEUTRAL', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1763476468, 'UPDATED_ON': 1763476469, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 43, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'cryptopolitan', 'NAME': 'Cryptopolitan', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://images.cryptocompare.com/news/default/cryptopolitan.png', 'URL': 'https://www.cryptopolitan.com/feed/', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': None, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 0, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1763476750, 'CREATED_ON': 1657730129, 'UPDATED_ON': 1681205909}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 5, 'NAME': 'ALTCOIN', 'CATEGORY': 'ALTCOIN'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 14, 'NAME': 'BTC', 'CATEGORY': 'BTC'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 26, 'NAME': 'FIAT', 'CATEGORY': 'FIAT'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 50, 'NAME': 'TRADING', 'CATEGORY': 'TRADING'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 211, 'NAME': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY', 'CATEGORY': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 54572532, 'GUID': 'https://www.cryptopolitan.com/?p=863280', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1763470800, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/43/54572532.jpeg', 'TITLE': 'Bitcoin Buyers Show Fatigue, But XRP Staking Platforms Are Only Just Getting Started', 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': 'Cryptopolitan Media', 'URL': 'https://www.cryptopolitan.com/bitcoin-buyers-show-fatigue-but-xrp-staking-platforms-are-only-just-getting-started/', 'SOURCE_ID': 43, 'BODY': 'Bitcoin’s short-term holder cohort has entered one of its steepest profitability declines of the cycle. With BTC now trading around $96,000, nearly all coins accumulated within the past 155 days are underwater. The shift from widespread profit to widespread loss is sharp, and it has left recent buyers without a clear short-term recovery path. These conditions often accompany late-stage drawdowns, where sentiment weakens and forced selling accelerates. As traders confront these pressures, attention is shifting to systems that operate on predictable mechanics rather than momentum. XRP staking is emerging as a focal point of that movement, particularly through platforms designed to provide structured yields and verifiable distribution. XRP Tundra sits at the center of this trend as its staking infrastructure and dual-token architecture gain visibility among users looking for well-defined alternatives. Bitcoin’s Short-Term Holders Face One of the Sharpest Profitability Drops in Years Glassnode data shows that short-term holder profitability has collapsed toward zero. Nearly 99% of all BTC purchased within the last 155 days is now at a loss, a condition typically associated with market fatigue. When this cohort stops seeing green, emotional resilience declines and liquidity becomes increasingly fragile. BTC’s fall from its $126,000 peak to the current $96,000 range has amplified this pressure. Combined with weaker macro visibility, fading expectations for a Federal Reserve rate cut, and the lingering effects of October’s liquidity shock, the market’s risk appetite has decreased significantly. The Fear & Greed Index sliding to 10 reflects that shift. During such periods, wealth preservation typically moves away from price-chasing and toward models based on structured returns. Fragile Sentiment Pushes Investors Toward Predictable Yield Systems In uncertain markets, investors gravitate toward yield architectures with defined mechanics. XRP Tundra’s staking environment has gained more attention for this reason. A recent analysis from Crypto Legends highlighted how capital tends to consolidate around ecosystems with verifiable infrastructure and predictable reward pathways during periods of heavy drawdown. The XRPL ecosystem benefits from ongoing institutional interest, strengthened liquidity through ETF flows, and increased visibility among investors looking for alternatives to volatile spot movements. Within that landscape, Tundra’s approach to staking — based on tiered APYs and a dual-token structure — gives participants a clear way to engage without relying on market momentum. XRP Tundra’s Cryo Vaults Offer a Structured Entry Into Long-Term Yield The Cryo Vault system introduces a set of staking tiers designed to accommodate multiple strategies: Liquid Staking Projected APY: 4–6% Commitment: None Withdrawal: Instant Minimum: 100 TUNDRA-S Balanced Staking Projected APY: 8–12% Commitment: 30 days Withdrawal: After lock-up Minimum: 500 TUNDRA-S Premium Staking Projected APY: 15–20% Commitment: 90 days Withdrawal: After lock-up Minimum: 1,000 TUNDRA-S For many investors, these tiered mechanics offer more clarity than the unpredictable conditions shaping the broader market. Tundra’s roadmap also includes XRP staking through Frost Keys, which will allow native XRP holders to access yield directly in an audited, multi-chain environment — a feature not previously available in XRPL-based ecosystems. These pathways give the project a defined approach to reward generation during a time when BTC’s short-term holders face deteriorating profitability. Dual-Token Architecture Gives Tundra Stability During Market Exhaustion The architecture behind XRP Tundra is another factor in its rising visibility. TUNDRA-S operates on Solana, where high-throughput execution supports staking logic and network activity. TUNDRA-X functions on the XRP Ledger, where deterministic settlement and low-failure consensus support governance and reserves. This division between execution and settlement contributes to operational stability. Verification strengthens it further. XRP Tundra’s contracts have undergone independent review through the Cyberscope audit , the Solidproof audit and the FreshCoins audit . The development team is fully identified through Vital Block KYC certification . As new participants compare ecosystems, the phrase is XRP Tundra legit now shows up frequently in research discussions referencing these documents. Presale Economics and the 2026 Burn Define the Platform’s Early-Stage Advantage Tundra’s presale model adds another layer of predictability. Phase 12 currently prices TUNDRA-S at $0.214 with a 8% bonus, while TUNDRA-X is allocated free at its $0.107 reference value. Confirmed listing prices — $2.50 for TUNDRA-S and $1.25 for TUNDRA-X — give participants a clear understanding of launch valuation. The presale remains open until January 12, 2026, when any unsold tokens will be permanently burned. TUNDRA-S and TUNDRA-X are then distributed through an automated dual-chain airdrop exactly one hour before Tundra-S goes live on Meteora and Tundra-X begins trading on Sologenic. These mechanics establish a predictable environment at a time when Bitcoin’s short-term holder dynamics reflect fragility. With staking infrastructure still in its early phase, Tundra’s trajectory differs meaningfully from the exhaustion visible across BTC’s most recent cohort of buyers. Follow XRP Tundra’s development as staking adoption grows and investors search for structured opportunities during Bitcoin’s late-cycle fatigue. Buy Tundra Now: official XRP Tundra website How To Buy Tundra: step-by-step guide Security and Trust: FreshCoins audit Join the Community: X/Twitter', 'KEYWORDS': 'Press Release', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'NEGATIVE', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1763476470, 'UPDATED_ON': 1763476470, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 43, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'cryptopolitan', 'NAME': 'Cryptopolitan', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://images.cryptocompare.com/news/default/cryptopolitan.png', 'URL': 'https://www.cryptopolitan.com/feed/', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': None, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 0, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1763476750, 'CREATED_ON': 1657730129, 'UPDATED_ON': 1681205909}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 14, 'NAME': 'BTC', 'CATEGORY': 'BTC'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 15, 'NAME': 'BUSINESS', 'CATEGORY': 'BUSINESS'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 37, 'NAME': 'MARKET', 'CATEGORY': 'MARKET'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 58, 'NAME': 'XRP', 'CATEGORY': 'XRP'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 211, 'NAME': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY', 'CATEGORY': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 54572468, 'GUID': 'https://u.today/top-xrp-trader-who-predicted-700-rally-says-parabolic-setup-is-back', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1763470800, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/64/54572468.jpeg', 'TITLE': 'Top XRP Trader Who Predicted 700% Rally Says Parabolic Setup Is Back', 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': 'U.Today', 'URL': 'https://u.today/top-xrp-trader-who-predicted-700-rally-says-parabolic-setup-is-back', 'SOURCE_ID': 64, 'BODY': 'XRP is pressing into the $2.45 barrier, and if this breakout is confirmed, the same 700% parabolic move seen in 2024 becomes possible again, predicts top trader who nailed it previously.', 'KEYWORDS': 'XRP', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'POSITIVE', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1763476427, 'UPDATED_ON': 1763476428, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 64, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'utoday', 'NAME': 'U.Today', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://images.cryptocompare.com/news/default/utoday.png', 'URL': 'https://u.today/cryptocompare.php', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': 1506816000, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 49, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1763476832, 'CREATED_ON': 1657730129, 'UPDATED_ON': 1745920032}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 50, 'NAME': 'TRADING', 'CATEGORY': 'TRADING'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 58, 'NAME': 'XRP', 'CATEGORY': 'XRP'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 211, 'NAME': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY', 'CATEGORY': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 54572528, 'GUID': 'https://www.cryptopolitan.com/?p=863332', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1763470731, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/43/54572528.jpeg', 'TITLE': 'Internet services, apps go down as Cloudflare suffers major outage', 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': 'Jai Hamid', 'URL': 'https://www.cryptopolitan.com/mass-outage-hits-cloudflare/', 'SOURCE_ID': 43, 'BODY': 'Chaos hit the internet this morning when Cloudflare broke at the worst possible time and dragged huge platforms down with it. The outage first began around 6:00 AM ET, when the company’s support portal provider started “experiencing issues,” according to what Cloudflare posted on its own status page. The timing lined up with a planned maintenance window at the company’s SCL (Santiago) data center, but Cloudflare didn’t say that this was the cause. What users saw was simple: pages failed, feeds wouldn’t load, and error screens took over the internet. Tracking outages across major platforms caused by Cloudflare The platforms hit were big names. People on X complained they could not refresh posts. Gamers trying to play League of Legends or Valorant saw reports pile up on downdetector. Even the Cloudflare status page itself began breaking down around 7:03 AM ET, losing its CSS styling while the company said its team was “continuing to investigate this issue.” The official wording earlier at 6:48 AM ET said the company was aware of a problem that “potentially impacts multiple customers” and that more information would come later. Users trying to work found themselves blocked from random corners of the internet. Anyone loading Canva ran into problems creating or saving content. People trying to access OpenAI bumped into messages telling them to “Please unblock challenges.cloudflare.com to proceed,” which also stopped access to ChatGPT. That message spread across many websites at once because the security layers Cloudflare normally uses to protect them were not working, even though the websites behind them stayed online. People online tried to figure out if the error screens meant they were blocked. They were not. The Cloudflare tools that usually filter traffic were the part breaking, not the users. The outage came fast, broke things fast, and hit global platforms at the same time, which is why the impact felt huge. Shares of Cloudflare had slid by more than 4% at the opening bell. Sharpen your strategy with mentorship + daily ideas - 30 days free access to our trading program', 'KEYWORDS': 'Tech|Canva|ChatGPT|Cloudflare|X', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'NEGATIVE', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1763476467, 'UPDATED_ON': 1763478753, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 43, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'cryptopolitan', 'NAME': 'Cryptopolitan', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://images.cryptocompare.com/news/default/cryptopolitan.png', 'URL': 'https://www.cryptopolitan.com/feed/', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': None, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 0, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1763476750, 'CREATED_ON': 1657730129, 'UPDATED_ON': 1681205909}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 15, 'NAME': 'BUSINESS', 'CATEGORY': 'BUSINESS'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 25, 'NAME': 'EXCHANGE', 'CATEGORY': 'EXCHANGE'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 50, 'NAME': 'TRADING', 'CATEGORY': 'TRADING'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 64, 'NAME': 'RESEARCH', 'CATEGORY': 'RESEARCH'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 211, 'NAME': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY', 'CATEGORY': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 54572722, 'GUID': 'https://en.coinotag.com/el-salvador-buys-1090-bitcoin-despite-imf-loan-pledge-raising-compliance-questions', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1763470712, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/77/default.png', 'TITLE': 'El Salvador Buys 1,090 Bitcoin Despite IMF Loan Pledge, Raising Compliance Questions', 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': 'COINOTAG', 'URL': 'https://en.coinotag.com/el-salvador-buys-1090-bitcoin-despite-imf-loan-pledge-raising-compliance-questions', 'SOURCE_ID': 77, 'BODY': 'El Salvador has acquired 1,090 Bitcoin valued at over $100 million, increasing its holdings to more than 7,474 BTC despite IMF commitments to limit public exposure under a $1.4 billion loan agreement, sparking concerns over fiscal risks and transparency. El Salvador’s Bitcoin Purchase: Government adds 1,090 BTC, boosting reserves to over $683 million amid market', 'KEYWORDS': 'Bitcoin|News', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'NEGATIVE', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1763476769, 'UPDATED_ON': None, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 77, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'coinotag', 'NAME': 'CoinOtag', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/77/default.png', 'URL': 'https://en.coinotag.com/feed/', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': None, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 0, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1763476834, 'CREATED_ON': 1686819961, 'UPDATED_ON': 1717748924}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 14, 'NAME': 'BTC', 'CATEGORY': 'BTC'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 37, 'NAME': 'MARKET', 'CATEGORY': 'MARKET'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 211, 'NAME': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY', 'CATEGORY': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 54570687, 'GUID': 'https://cryptonews.com/?p=453045', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1763470592, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/52/54570687.jpeg', 'TITLE': 'S&P 500 Set for Longest Losing Streak Since August as Bitcoin Falls Below $90K', 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': 'Amin Ayan', 'URL': 'https://cryptonews.com/news/sp-500-set-for-longest-losing-streak-since-august-as-bitcoin-falls-below-90k/', 'SOURCE_ID': 52, 'BODY': 'The S&P 500 is on track for a fourth consecutive decline as mounting concerns over Federal Reserve policy, shaky confidence in artificial intelligence valuations and a sharp downturn in Bitcoin weigh on global markets. Key Takeaways: The S&P 500 is heading for its fourth straight decline as Fed uncertainty, AI valuation fears and Bitcoin’s drop below $90,000 rattle markets. US stocks now trade at stretched valuations, with the S&P 500 at 22x forward earnings. Traders are bracing for Nvidia’s earnings and key labor data. Futures tied to the benchmark index slipped 0.4% early Tuesday in New York, pointing toward the longest losing streak since late August. Nasdaq 100 futures also fell 0.4%, mirroring losses across Asian and European markets. Bitcoin added to the risk-off mood, briefly dropping below $90,000 for the first time in seven months. AI Valuation Jitters and Shutdown Fears Drag Down US Stocks US equities have been under pressure throughout November, with investors increasingly uneasy about whether the AI trade has pushed valuations too far. The S&P 500 now trades at roughly 22 times forward earnings, well above its decade-long average of 19. Sentiment has also been dragged lower by concerns surrounding the economic fallout from the longest US government shutdown on record. “Appetite for AI is under pressure from circularity worries and bubble fears,” Ipek Ozkardeskaya, senior analyst at Swissquote, told Bloomberg on Tuesday . “The bad news is that some of the more bullish vibes — AI enthusiasm, massive government stimulus, dovish central-bank expectations — are starting to fade.” Despite the recent weakness, dip-buying has remained active. The S&P 500 managed to reverse sharp losses on Friday, recovering from a 1.4% slide to finish nearly flat. Still, options data shows growing demand for bearish hedges in the tech sector, signaling a cooling of confidence in the sustainability of the recent rally. Bitcoin is right now leading S&P500 by 15 days That fits Quantpedia’s 2023 finding, Bitcoin leads equities 10–20 days during liquidity regime transitions (risk-on to risk-off) If equities stall next week, the next leg’s likely down pic.twitter.com/E3wkJv2GVv — Miad Kasravi (@ZFXtrading) November 16, 2025 The S&P 500 now sits about 3% below its October high and on Monday closed under its 50-day moving average for the first time since April, a level many traders view as a key marker of short-term momentum. The next catalyst may arrive Wednesday when Nvidia reports quarterly earnings, a critical moment for assessing whether the AI trade still has fuel. Meanwhile, swaps markets show traders reducing expectations for a Fed rate cut in December. “We believe that the nervousness will persist until the September employment report provides greater clarity,” said Homin Lee, senior macro strategist at Lombard Odier. “At the current juncture, a soft US labor market data or a large beat in Nvidia earnings could help.” Bitcoin Crashes Below $90K as ETF Investors Face First Losses Bitcoin plunged under $90,000 on Tuesday for the first time since April, erasing its entire 2025 rally and sending the average spot ETF investor into the red. The drop pushed Bitcoin more than 30% below its early-October record, marking the first time ETF inflows, now sitting at a flow-weighted cost basis of about $89,600, have collectively turned negative . The downturn triggered a wave of ETF outflows, with November 17 alone seeing $254 million exit US Bitcoin funds, led by large redemptions from BlackRock’s IBIT and GBTC. Bitcoin dominance also slipped below 60% as Ether fell under $3,000 and major altcoins, including XRP, BNB, and Solana, posted losses of up to 5.6%, signaling broad market stress. The post S&P 500 Set for Longest Losing Streak Since August as Bitcoin Falls Below $90K appeared first on Cryptonews .', 'KEYWORDS': 'Bitcoin News|Bitcoin|Market|S&P', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'NEGATIVE', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1763470686, 'UPDATED_ON': 1763470686, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 52, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'cryptonews', 'NAME': 'cryptonews', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://images.cryptocompare.com/news/default/cryptonews.png', 'URL': 'https://cryptonews.com/news/feed/', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': None, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 0, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1763476754, 'CREATED_ON': 1657730129, 'UPDATED_ON': 1680604053}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 14, 'NAME': 'BTC', 'CATEGORY': 'BTC'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 37, 'NAME': 'MARKET', 'CATEGORY': 'MARKET'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 50, 'NAME': 'TRADING', 'CATEGORY': 'TRADING'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 210, 'NAME': 'MACROECONOMICS', 'CATEGORY': 'MACROECONOMICS'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 211, 'NAME': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY', 'CATEGORY': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 54570593, 'GUID': 'https://bitcoinworld.co.in/?p=220342', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1763470511, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/82/default.png', 'TITLE': 'Revolutionary Crypto Regulatory Framework: Brazil’s Bold 2026 Digital Asset Transformation', 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': 'Editorial Team', 'URL': 'https://bitcoinworld.co.in/brazil-crypto-regulatory-framework/', 'SOURCE_ID': 82, 'BODY': 'BitcoinWorld Revolutionary Crypto Regulatory Framework: Brazil’s Bold 2026 Digital Asset Transformation Brazil is making groundbreaking moves in the cryptocurrency space with its upcoming crypto regulatory framework set for February 2026. This comprehensive approach positions Brazil as a Latin American leader in digital asset regulation. The Central Bank of Brazil’s announcement marks a significant milestone for investors and businesses operating in the crypto space. What Does Brazil’s New Crypto Regulatory Framework Include? The Brazilian government has outlined three key implementing resolutions that will shape the country’s digital asset landscape. This crypto regulatory framework represents one of the most comprehensive approaches in the region. The measures aim to balance innovation with consumer protection and financial stability. According to Chainalysis, Brazil ranks among the top cryptocurrency markets globally. Therefore, this regulatory framework comes at a crucial time. The Central Bank of Brazil (BCB) has carefully designed these regulations to address multiple aspects of the crypto ecosystem. Key Components of Brazil’s Crypto Transformation The new framework introduces several important changes that will affect how crypto businesses operate. These measures demonstrate Brazil’s commitment to creating a secure and transparent digital asset market. New Licensing Process – Crypto-related businesses must obtain proper authorization Enhanced AML/CFT Rules – Stronger anti-money laundering and counter-terrorism financing requirements Customer Asset Protection – Mandatory segregation of client funds from company assets This crypto regulatory framework ensures that Brazil keeps pace with global standards. Moreover, it provides much-needed clarity for both domestic and international investors. Why is Brazil’s Crypto Regulatory Framework Important? The implementation of this comprehensive crypto regulatory framework addresses several critical needs in the market. First, it establishes clear rules for businesses operating in the cryptocurrency space. Second, it enhances consumer confidence by implementing robust protection measures. Brazil’s approach to cryptocurrency regulation could serve as a model for other emerging markets. The February 2026 timeline gives businesses adequate preparation time. Consequently, this gradual implementation allows for smooth adaptation to the new requirements. Benefits and Challenges of the New Framework The crypto regulatory framework brings numerous advantages to Brazil’s financial ecosystem. However, it also presents some challenges that market participants must address. Increased Investor Confidence – Clear rules attract institutional investment Reduced Fraud Risk – Enhanced oversight minimizes fraudulent activities Global Compliance – Alignment with international regulatory standards Implementation Costs – Businesses face compliance expenses Adaptation Period – Companies need time to adjust to new requirements This balanced approach to the crypto regulatory framework shows Brazil’s understanding of both opportunities and risks in the digital asset space. What to Expect Before February 2026? The period leading to February 2026 will see significant preparation across Brazil’s cryptocurrency industry. Businesses should begin assessing their current operations against the proposed requirements. The Central Bank will likely provide additional guidance and clarification in the coming months. This crypto regulatory framework represents a pivotal moment for Brazil’s financial technology sector. It demonstrates the country’s commitment to embracing digital innovation while maintaining financial stability and consumer protection. Conclusion: Brazil’s Strategic Move in Global Crypto Landscape Brazil’s upcoming crypto regulatory framework positions the country as a forward-thinking player in the global digital economy. By February 2026, Brazil will have established one of Latin America’s most comprehensive cryptocurrency regulatory systems. This framework balances innovation with necessary safeguards, potentially setting a benchmark for other nations. The careful planning and phased implementation show Brazil’s strategic approach to cryptocurrency regulation. This move could significantly influence how emerging markets approach digital asset regulation in the future. Frequently Asked Questions When does Brazil’s new crypto regulatory framework take effect? The framework officially launches in February 2026, giving businesses nearly two years to prepare for compliance. What types of businesses need licensing under the new framework? All cryptocurrency exchanges, trading platforms, and digital asset service providers operating in Brazil will require proper licensing. How will customer asset protection work? The framework mandates segregation of customer assets from company funds, similar to traditional financial institution requirements. Will the new regulations affect individual cryptocurrency investors? Individual investors will benefit from enhanced protections, but won’t face additional regulatory burdens beyond existing tax obligations. How does Brazil’s approach compare to other countries? Brazil’s framework is more comprehensive than many emerging markets and aligns closely with developed market standards. Can international crypto businesses operate in Brazil under the new framework? Yes, but they must comply with the same licensing and regulatory requirements as domestic companies. Found this article insightful? Help spread awareness about Brazil’s groundbreaking crypto regulatory framework by sharing this piece on your social media channels. Your shares help educate more people about these important financial developments! To learn more about the latest cryptocurrency trends, explore our article on key developments shaping digital assets institutional adoption. This post Revolutionary Crypto Regulatory Framework: Brazil’s Bold 2026 Digital Asset Transformation first appeared on BitcoinWorld .', 'KEYWORDS': 'Crypto News|Blockchain Policy|Brazil cryptocurrency|Crypto Regulation.|Digital Assets|Financial Compliance', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'POSITIVE', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1763470559, 'UPDATED_ON': None, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 82, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'bitcoinworld', 'NAME': 'Bitcoin World', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/82/default.png', 'URL': 'https://bitcoinworld.co.in/feed/', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': None, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 0, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1763476746, 'CREATED_ON': 1698066984, 'UPDATED_ON': 1747932437}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 15, 'NAME': 'BUSINESS', 'CATEGORY': 'BUSINESS'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 37, 'NAME': 'MARKET', 'CATEGORY': 'MARKET'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 41, 'NAME': 'REGULATION', 'CATEGORY': 'REGULATION'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 210, 'NAME': 'MACROECONOMICS', 'CATEGORY': 'MACROECONOMICS'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 211, 'NAME': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY', 'CATEGORY': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 54570744, 'GUID': 'https://en.coinotag.com/ukraine-aims-to-build-sovereign-ai-infrastructure-with-nvidia-partnership', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1763470458, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/77/default.png', 'TITLE': 'Ukraine Aims to Build Sovereign AI Infrastructure with Nvidia Partnership', 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': 'COINOTAG', 'URL': 'https://en.coinotag.com/ukraine-aims-to-build-sovereign-ai-infrastructure-with-nvidia-partnership', 'SOURCE_ID': 77, 'BODY': 'Ukraine is partnering with Nvidia to build sovereign artificial intelligence infrastructure, enhancing national security and data protection while advancing AI education and research. This initiative supports the country’s digital transformation, including ties to blockchain testing and virtual asset regulations for a robust crypto ecosystem. Key collaboration: Ukraine and Nvidia are developing state-controlled AI using advanced', 'KEYWORDS': 'News', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'POSITIVE', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1763470789, 'UPDATED_ON': None, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 77, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'coinotag', 'NAME': 'CoinOtag', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/77/default.png', 'URL': 'https://en.coinotag.com/feed/', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': None, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 0, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1763476834, 'CREATED_ON': 1686819961, 'UPDATED_ON': 1717748924}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 13, 'NAME': 'BLOCKCHAIN', 'CATEGORY': 'BLOCKCHAIN'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 64, 'NAME': 'RESEARCH', 'CATEGORY': 'RESEARCH'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 211, 'NAME': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY', 'CATEGORY': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 54570619, 'GUID': 'https://en.coinotag.com/breakingnews/ethereum-set-for-major-cex-liquidations-1-055b-short-liquidation-strength-if-it-breaks-3150-and-797m-long-liquidation-strength-if-it-falls-to-2950', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1763470443, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/77/default.png', 'TITLE': '🚨 Ethereum Set for Major CEX Liquidations: $1.055B Short Liquidation Strength If It Breaks $3,150 and $797M Long Liquidation Strength If It Falls to $2,950', 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': 'COINOTAG', 'URL': 'https://en.coinotag.com/breakingnews/ethereum-set-for-major-cex-liquidations-1-055b-short-liquidation-strength-if-it-breaks-3150-and-797m-long-liquidation-strength-if-it-falls-to-2950', 'SOURCE_ID': 77, 'BODY': 'Ethereum Set for Major CEX Liquidations: $1.055B Short Liquidation Strength If It Breaks $3,150 and $797M Long Liquidation Strength If It Falls to $2,950', 'KEYWORDS': 'Breaking News', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'NEUTRAL', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1763470583, 'UPDATED_ON': None, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 77, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'coinotag', 'NAME': 'CoinOtag', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/77/default.png', 'URL': 'https://en.coinotag.com/feed/', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': None, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 0, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1763476834, 'CREATED_ON': 1686819961, 'UPDATED_ON': 1717748924}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 24, 'NAME': 'ETH', 'CATEGORY': 'ETH'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 211, 'NAME': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY', 'CATEGORY': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 54570561, 'GUID': 'https://seekingalpha.com/article/4844988-msty-understanding-its-performance-and-potential?utm_source=cryptocompare.com&utm_medium=referral&feed_item_type=article', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1763470386, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/50/54570561.jpeg', 'TITLE': 'MSTY: Understanding Its Performance And Potential', 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': '', 'URL': 'https://seekingalpha.com/article/4844988-msty-understanding-its-performance-and-potential?utm_source=cryptocompare.com&utm_medium=referral&feed_item_type=article', 'SOURCE_ID': 50, 'BODY': \"Summary YieldMax MSTR Option Income Strategy ETF (MSTY) offers high income via covered calls on volatile MSTR, but has suffered alongside MSTR's decline. MSTY's recent price drop is tied to MSTR's weakness and market volatility, not just NAV erosion, with distributions still attractive for income seekers. MSTY is best used as a small, aggressive allocation within a diversified income portfolio, not as a core holding due to its risk profile. Current MSTY price presents a more favorable entry point; upside is tied to a rebound in Bitcoin and MSTR, with less risk of NAV erosion now. YieldMax MSTR Option Income Strategy ETF ( MSTY ) is among the more well known of the synthetic covered call ETFS. Not only is it highly covered and commented upon, but it also has $2.25 billion in assets under management ( AUM ) and trading volume of approximately 18 million daily. The primary purpose of the ETF is to generate income using a covered call strategy with the underlying stock being Strategy Inc. ( MSTR ), which has been out of favor since the middle of July, losing over half of its market cap during that time. From the latter part of February 2025 to mid-August 2025, MSTY had a nice run, paying out high distributions while retaining its NAV. Since August 19, 2025 however, when the share price broke below its six-month floor, it has continued to drop in conjunction with MSTR, resulting in a new 52-week low below $8.00 per share. NAV erosion or response to the underlying? Interestingly, as the chart below shows, MSTY didn't break away much from the share price movement of MSTR, mirroring most of that movement without getting crushed. That suggests to me that MSTY isn't simply dropping because of NAV erosion, by which I mean paying out more than the covered calls are generating in income. MSTY chart (Seeking Alpha) To the contrary, I think it's a combination of the performance of the underlying, along with the high distributions being paid out. When studying MSTY and other covered call ETFs, the one thing that can be counted on is the quality of the underlying stock management is writing options against. In the case of MSTR, we know it's a volatile stock that many think has yet to prove its Bitcoin strategy is sustainable long term. For that reason, there's lot of volatility coming from the swings in the price of Bitcoin. And when adding macro elements like increasing chatter about a recession and uncertainty as to how committed the Federal Reserve is in regard to continuing to lower interest rates, it has created a perfect storm of concern and fear that has, in my opinion, had a disproportionate impact on MSTR, and by extension, MSTY. Until that works itself out, I think we're not going to see and price discovery on the low side for MSTY, which would result in potential investors to take a position in, or increase their position in the ETF. Also, we're seeing more of the opposite, with those holding the ETF panicking and rushing toward the exits. What has changed with Bitcoin A major reason for the continual volatility is that there are new players in town in contrast to the retail investors of the past that were committed hodlers. That has changed, not only with large institutional investors and retail whales, but also a new breed of trader that moves in and out of Bitcoin and other cryptos in order to take advantage of short-term price swings. It appears to me that there are a small portion of institutional investors and whales that are precipitating some of this, and that has had an impact on the fear trade and wild price movement of Bitcoin, MSTR, and MSTY. Over the long term that's going to change, as there are a growing number of institutional investors and retail whales that are taking positions in Bitcoin for the long term. I see that, over time, having the prolonged impact on Bitcoin, which will lend support to MSTR, and MSTY will be the beneficiary of that. Also, we need to take into account that when the big rebound comes for MSTR, that MSTY isn't going to participate in the upside of the price movement to the same degree as Strategy does. Nonetheless, what will happen is it should be able to boost its distributions as the price of MSTR returns to strong growth again. At that time I think we'll have price discovery for the ETF and a consistently accurate expectation as to its performance. MSTY disributions (Seeking Alpha) Volatility will of course remain in play, but the price will continue to move up in conjunction with Bitcoin and MSTR, providing those seeking income a nice return, albeit not at the same pace. That day isn't here yet, but once we see the rebound in Bitcoin we'll get a much clearer look at how MSTY is going to perform under that new environment. How I see the best-case scenario going forward for MSTY is, after Bitcoin and MSTR reverse direction, MSTY will probably start to trade sideways with a slight upward movement in its share price. The degree of that upward movement should be connected to the distribution being paid out. Part of a portfolio Online I've seen people on various social platforms state that they're allocating significant percentages of their investment capital in high-yield ETFs like MSTY, thinking they're hastening their goal toward financial independence. This is a very risky strategy to employ in the income-generating segment of the market. An ETF like MSTY should be part of portfolio of income-producing investment instruments, with a balanced number of ETFs or other securities representing a spectrum of safer and more aggressive holdings. It would be wise to have a foundational strategy of low-risk ETFs that include at least one that tracks the S&P 500 and the Nasdaq. There are of course different things to consider when putting together a portfolio of income-producing ETFs, including age, risk factors, and retirement goals, among other things. But to buy one high-yielding ETF like MSTY as a significant percentage of an overall income portfolio is playing with fire. I like MSTY as the more aggressive part of an income portfolio, yet it should only reflect a relatively small percentage of the weighting of the basket of ETFs. Conclusion I don't blame investors for getting concerned over the drop in price of MSTY, especially if they have a much higher cost basis than it is currently trading at. A couple months ago I sold my shares because I believed the share price was going to steeply drop, and it has. I had enjoyed a nice return during the period of time when MSTY was paying out solid distributions while retaining NAV. The high distribution levels easily overcame the drop in share price, but I correctly assumed it was going to be difficult to do so in the near term. My cost basis was slightly over $20.00 per share when I sold, and it has dropped by over $12.00 per share from that point as I write. What I figured was it would take a long time to recoup my capital, not only from the drop in share price but from what I expected would be drop in distributions at the same time. That has also came to pass, so now I'm in a waiting pattern until the bottom of Bitcoin comes in and confirmation it has hit the floor during this period of time is clear and confirmed. Once that happens, I will seriously look at opening another position in MSTY. At the current price point of the ETF, I'm not too concerned about NAV erosion. I'm more interested in how management responds to the inevitable return to Bitcoin price growth, and how well they do in generating income from covered calls in an environment that returns to growth in the price of Bitcoin and the underlying. Finally, when the price of MSTR reverses direction, I think MSTY management will start to pay out higher distributions again, taking into account they'll fluctuate week to week based upon MSTR's response to the price movement of Bitcoin. For that reason, I think the price MSTY is trading at now is close to a good entry point. The downside is much less than when it was trading earlier in the year, and assuming my thesis concerning distributions is correct, it should be a much better holding for income generation than it was in the past, with less risk concerning NAV erosion.\", 'KEYWORDS': 'MSTY', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'NEUTRAL', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1763470473, 'UPDATED_ON': 1763470474, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 50, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'seekingalpha', 'NAME': 'Seeking Alpha', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://images.cryptocompare.com/news/default/seekingalpha.png', 'URL': 'https://seekingalpha.com/feeds/cryptocompare/cryptos', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': None, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 0, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1763476842, 'CREATED_ON': 1657730129, 'UPDATED_ON': 1673257636}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 14, 'NAME': 'BTC', 'CATEGORY': 'BTC'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 15, 'NAME': 'BUSINESS', 'CATEGORY': 'BUSINESS'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 50, 'NAME': 'TRADING', 'CATEGORY': 'TRADING'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 210, 'NAME': 'MACROECONOMICS', 'CATEGORY': 'MACROECONOMICS'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 211, 'NAME': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY', 'CATEGORY': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 54570464, 'GUID': 'https://en.bitcoinsistemi.com/santiment-announced-bitcoin-btc-xrp-and-these-three-altcoins-are-in-historic-buy-zones/', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1763470330, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/81/54570464.jpeg', 'TITLE': 'Santiment Announced: \"Bitcoin (BTC), XRP and These Three Altcoins Are in Historic Buy Zones!\"', 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': 'Elif Azra Güven', 'URL': 'https://en.bitcoinsistemi.com/santiment-announced-bitcoin-btc-xrp-and-these-three-altcoins-are-in-historic-buy-zones/', 'SOURCE_ID': 81, 'BODY': 'Bitcoin (BTC) and altcoins are continuing their downward trend. At this point, Bitcoin has fallen below $90,000 for the first time in seven months, a decline that has dragged the entire cryptocurrency market into negative territory for the week. Analyzing the latest situation in BTC and altcoins, analysis platform Santiment said that data suggests it may be a good time to take advantage of the decline for some cryptocurrencies and consider buying. According to Santiment, Bitcoin, Cardano (ADA), Chainlink (LINK), Ethereum (ETH), and XRP present buying opportunities. At this point, Santiment said in his post that most major cryptocurrencies have become unprofitable for short-term investors. According to Santiment, wallets that purchased Cardano, Chainlink, Ethereum, Bitcoin, and XRP in the last 30 days are experiencing a decline of over 10% in their portfolios, indicating a significant drop in average transaction returns. Using the MVRV ratio in his analysis of the “buy signal on a dip,” Santiment stated that the relevant cryptocurrencies should be purchased when their returns are extremely negative. “According to Santiment data; Cardano – ADA: -19.7% (Overbought Zone) Chainlink – LINK: -16.8% (Overbought Zone) Ethereum- ETH: -15.4% (Overbought Zone) Bitcoin- BTC: -11.5% (Good Buy Zone) XRP: -10.2% (Good Buy Zone) is giving a buy signal. Santiment recently noted that the MVRV ratio is a good metric for identifying buy zones. While support and resistance levels provide similar context, the MVRV offers a more accurate reference, according to Santiment. “…In a zero-sum game, buy assets when the average trading returns of your peers are extremely negative. The lower the MVRV ratios, the greater the likelihood of a rapid recovery.” *This is not investment advice. Continue Reading: Santiment Announced: \"Bitcoin (BTC), XRP and These Three Altcoins Are in Historic Buy Zones!\"', 'KEYWORDS': 'Altcoin|Analysis|Bitcoin|Cardano|Ethereum|News|XRP', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'NEUTRAL', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1763470349, 'UPDATED_ON': 1763470349, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 81, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'bitcoinsistemi', 'NAME': 'BitcoinSistemi', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/81/default.png', 'URL': 'https://en.bitcoinsistemi.com/feed/', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': None, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 0, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1763476746, 'CREATED_ON': 1692873798, 'UPDATED_ON': 1692873836}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 3, 'NAME': 'ADA', 'CATEGORY': 'ADA'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 5, 'NAME': 'ALTCOIN', 'CATEGORY': 'ALTCOIN'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 14, 'NAME': 'BTC', 'CATEGORY': 'BTC'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 58, 'NAME': 'XRP', 'CATEGORY': 'XRP'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 211, 'NAME': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY', 'CATEGORY': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 54570324, 'GUID': 'https://seekingalpha.com/article/4844985-iren-a-40-percent-pullback-in-a-3-4b-arr-future?utm_source=cryptocompare.com&utm_medium=referral&feed_item_type=article', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1763469947, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/50/54570324.jpeg', 'TITLE': 'IREN: A 40% Pullback In A $3.4B ARR Future', 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': '', 'URL': 'https://seekingalpha.com/article/4844985-iren-a-40-percent-pullback-in-a-3-4b-arr-future?utm_source=cryptocompare.com&utm_medium=referral&feed_item_type=article', 'SOURCE_ID': 50, 'BODY': \"Summary IREN Limited is a rapidly growing dual data center business with a unique blend of Bitcoin mining and AI/HPC hosting operations. IREN's vertical integration, secured 2.9GW power capacity, and strong financing position it well for future growth, despite recent share price volatility. Valuation suggests significant upside potential if execution matches guidance, with a forward P/S ratio becoming attractive by 2027. After a 40% dip, I initiate IREN at a Strong Buy, citing improved risk-reward, but note elevated risks tied to execution, competition, and macroeconomic conditions. Introduction IREN Limited ( IREN ) has been one of the hottest stocks in the market since its 1,300%+ rally from April lows to November highs. Since November 5, however, shares have been in a somewhat steep downtrend, declining approximately 40% from their all-time high. Since IREN is a stock that has been on my watch list for quite some time now, I figured it was time to dive deeper and evaluate whether said drop is an investment opportunity or not. IREN is a rapidly growing dual data center business that has both Bitcoin mining and AI/HPC hosting operations while owning the infrastructure. They have secured 2.9GW of power capacity. The recent drop can be seen as a slight reset in sentiment, as fears of a popping AI bubble , which first takes a hit on sharply risen, highly valued, and currently unprofitable stocks with more uncertainty and reliance on future developments such as IREN. This finally gives new investors an opportunity to start building a first position in the company, as the risk-reward profile has improved. Their recently posted Q1 FY2026 results underscore this, as many authors on Seeking Alpha as well as other news outlets have already covered them. The image below will therefore be enough coverage on that topic from me today. IREN IR The Good IREN is vertically integrated with roughly 2.9 GW of secured power, more than any peer in the AI-pivoting data-center space. Because they own their data centers end-to-end, including land, substations, cooling, and shells, they avoid landlord markups and can shift capacity between Bitcoin mining and AI hosting as economics change. Another unique advantage for IREN is their capability of superior financing for their project buildouts. They have $1.8B in cash on their balance sheet, positive operating cash flows, and the Microsoft prepayment (and future ones in other deals) can be employed before taking on further debt or diluting shareholders. IREN IR Their Bitcoin mining has strong unit economics, at least at current prices, having an all-in cost to mine around $40k when Bitcoin trades above $90k. A real risk I do see is Bitcoin having a very bad 2026, as cycle theory (which it has so far followed and is yet to break) suggests. In that case, I could see prices closing in on IREN's cost to mine, which would erode any earnings and cash flows to use for their buildouts. In that case, however, it is still handy to have the flexible data center structure so they can allocate more compute to AI hosting, and even if some mining operations continue, they would 1) not generate large losses, as I believe it is highly unlikely for Bitcoin to drop below $30k again, and 2) have the possibility to still be profitable in the long run with rising Bitcoin prices (if they hold onto some of the coins). Due to owning the whole stack and likely boasting longer-term customer relationships, I expect IREN's future margins to top those of its data center peers, as the MSFT deal at an anticipated 85% EBITDA margin exemplifies. IREN IR One negative aspect, though, is that IREN is not a leader in AI cloud and is far behind CRWV and NBIS, as a rating by SemiAnalysis (November 2025) has IREN as underperforming, whereas its peers are at the top. SemiAnalysis Another key investment thesis component is further deals that will be announced in the future. I do not believe that we have seen the height of this market and that we will have many more contracts on the way. This is also confirmed by a recent conversation between Sundar Pichai and Elon Musk on X. X Valuation On a P/S ratio, IREN trades at 18, which is an elevated multiple on an absolute basis and also much higher than CoreWeave ( CRWV ) at 7.5, though much lower than Nebius Group N.V. ( NBIS ) at 55. Data by YCharts IREN anticipates $3.4B in ARR by the end of 2026. That means they will earn $3.4B / 4 = $850M in Q4 CY2026 (their Q2 FY2027). At 50% QoQ growth due to their contract ramp, the previous quarters could look something like this: Q3 = 850 / 1.50 = $567MQ2 = 567 / 1.50 = $378MQ1 = 378 / 1.50 = $252M ... leading to total 2026 revenues of $2.05B, or a forward P/S ratio of 6.4. Assuming YoY growth of 80% from there leaves us with $3.7B in revenue in CY2027. This mostly ignores Bitcoin mining revenue, but as the company is transitioning and we want a margin of safety, let's value IREN solely based on their AI revenues. That means that in 2027, IREN would trade at a P/S ratio of 3.5 if the price did not move one inch from today. In contrast, CRWV trades at a 2027 P/S ratio of 2 and NBIS at around 4, which makes all of them seem undervalued. If data center growth is not expected to slow down before 2030 and considering the recent rapid growth of all major data center players, I do believe that IREN will continue to grow beyond 2027, though not at a pace of 80%+. Still, that should lead to them being valued like a growth stock, and if solid margins can manifest (or are foreseeable) until then, they surely deserve a P/S of at least 7. This implies upside potential of 100% in our valuation over a two-year horizon. Risks Despite the share price drop, IREN remains a higher-risk investment. Key caveats start with their high beta and cyclicality in an already record-highly valued market. In the short term, high valuations cannot accurately forecast results, but in the longer term they can do so well, meaning that dedicated, high-quality company stock picking at reasonable prices will be key. If we see a broader selloff, a recession, or risk-off environment, key winners like IREN would be the ones to drop the most, though that then might become a great buying opportunity. Another significant factor is execution risk from already priced in future revenues. IREN's growth depends on timely completion of large, complex liquid cooling data center projects such as Horizon 1, Horizon 2, and Sweetwater. Delays, cost overruns, or technical challenges could impact operating capacity and revenue realization, but also financing. Continued dilution and/or too much debt at too high interest rates worsen investors future returns by making every share less valuable and increasing risks of bankruptcy. Lastly, growing competition in such a rapidly expanding market is to be expected. A more competitive environment can foster lower prices that customers can be charged, leading to lower revenues and margins. Conclusion Since a lot of the valuation today is based on future execution, buildouts, and revenues, IREN's risks are elevated. Still, after this 40% dip, the risk-reward profile has improved and leaves upside potential if execution matches guidance, which makes me initiate IREN at a Strong Buy rating. This rating is subject to short-term change, as it depends a lot on macroeconomic developments and the broader state of the market with respect to the AI trade. In that given case, I might provide updates in the comments. Rating: Initiate Strong Buy.\", 'KEYWORDS': 'IREN', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'POSITIVE', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1763470005, 'UPDATED_ON': 1763470473, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 50, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'seekingalpha', 'NAME': 'Seeking Alpha', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://images.cryptocompare.com/news/default/seekingalpha.png', 'URL': 'https://seekingalpha.com/feeds/cryptocompare/cryptos', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': None, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 0, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1763476842, 'CREATED_ON': 1657730129, 'UPDATED_ON': 1673257636}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 14, 'NAME': 'BTC', 'CATEGORY': 'BTC'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 15, 'NAME': 'BUSINESS', 'CATEGORY': 'BUSINESS'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 37, 'NAME': 'MARKET', 'CATEGORY': 'MARKET'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 39, 'NAME': 'MINING', 'CATEGORY': 'MINING'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 211, 'NAME': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY', 'CATEGORY': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 54570433, 'GUID': 'https://bitcoinworld.co.in/?p=220335', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1763469911, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/82/default.png', 'TITLE': 'Decred Price Prediction 2025-2030: Will DCR Shatter the $50 Barrier?', 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': 'Sofiya', 'URL': 'https://bitcoinworld.co.in/decred-price-prediction-2030/', 'SOURCE_ID': 82, 'BODY': 'BitcoinWorld Decred Price Prediction 2025-2030: Will DCR Shatter the $50 Barrier? As cryptocurrency markets continue to evolve, Decred (DCR) stands out as a unique project with hybrid consensus mechanism and strong governance model. Investors are increasingly curious about the Decred price prediction for the coming years, particularly whether DCR can break through the crucial $50 resistance level. This comprehensive analysis examines the factors that could drive DCR’s price movement through 2025 and beyond. What Makes Decred Different From Other Cryptocurrencies? Decred represents a sophisticated approach to blockchain technology that combines Proof-of-Work and Proof-of-Stake systems. This hybrid consensus mechanism ensures network security while maintaining democratic governance. Unlike many cryptocurrencies, Decred gives token holders direct voting power on protocol changes and treasury management. Current DCR Market Position and Technical Analysis The DCR cryptocurrency has demonstrated resilience during market fluctuations. Current technical indicators suggest: Strong support levels between $15-$20 Consistent trading volume despite market volatility Growing institutional interest in the project’s unique value proposition Decred Price Prediction 2025: The Path to $50 Our 2025 Decred price prediction considers multiple factors including adoption rates, technological developments, and overall market conditions. Key drivers include: Factor Impact Probability Mainnet upgrades High 85% Exchange listings Medium 70% Partnership announcements Medium 65% Long-Term DCR Cryptocurrency Forecast 2026-2030 The extended forecast for this digital currency projects gradual growth driven by: Enhanced privacy features implementation Growing decentralized governance adoption Increasing recognition as a store of value Why Decred Represents a Compelling Crypto Investment For investors seeking exposure to innovative blockchain technology , Decred offers several advantages. The project’s treasury system provides sustainable funding for development, while its governance model prevents contentious hard forks that have plagued other cryptocurrencies. Risks and Challenges for DCR Price Growth While the Decred price prediction appears optimistic, investors should consider potential challenges: Regulatory uncertainty affecting all cryptocurrencies Competition from other governance-focused projects Market volatility impacting short-term price movements Expert Insights on DCR Cryptocurrency Future Industry analysts remain cautiously optimistic about this digital currency . The project’s fundamental strengths in governance and sustainability position it well for long-term growth, though immediate price targets depend heavily on broader market conditions. Frequently Asked Questions What is Decred’s current circulating supply? Decred has a fixed maximum supply of 21 million coins, with approximately 70% currently in circulation. How does Decred’s governance system work? DCR holders can stake their coins to participate in voting on protocol changes and treasury spending. Where can I buy DCR cryptocurrency? Decred is available on major exchanges including Binance , Coinbase , and Kraken . Who founded Decred? Decred was initiated by developers from Company 0 , including well-known figures in the cryptocurrency space. Decred’s unique approach to blockchain governance and sustainable development makes it a standout project in the crowded cryptocurrency space. While breaking the $50 barrier will require favorable market conditions and continued project development, the fundamental strengths of the DCR cryptocurrency suggest it has the potential to achieve significant growth through 2030. The project’s commitment to decentralized decision-making and technological innovation positions it well for long-term success in the evolving digital currency landscape. To learn more about the latest cryptocurrency markets trends, explore our article on key developments shaping Decred and other digital currencies institutional adoption. This post Decred Price Prediction 2025-2030: Will DCR Shatter the $50 Barrier? first appeared on BitcoinWorld .', 'KEYWORDS': 'Crypto News|BLOCKCHAIN|CRYPTOCURRENCY|Decred|Investment|PRICE PREDICTION', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'POSITIVE', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1763470266, 'UPDATED_ON': None, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 82, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'bitcoinworld', 'NAME': 'Bitcoin World', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/82/default.png', 'URL': 'https://bitcoinworld.co.in/feed/', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': None, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 0, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1763476746, 'CREATED_ON': 1698066984, 'UPDATED_ON': 1747932437}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 13, 'NAME': 'BLOCKCHAIN', 'CATEGORY': 'BLOCKCHAIN'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 25, 'NAME': 'EXCHANGE', 'CATEGORY': 'EXCHANGE'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 37, 'NAME': 'MARKET', 'CATEGORY': 'MARKET'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 50, 'NAME': 'TRADING', 'CATEGORY': 'TRADING'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 211, 'NAME': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY', 'CATEGORY': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 54572543, 'GUID': 'https://cryptopotato.com/?p=1420504', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1763469776, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://images.cryptocompare.com/news/default/cryptopotato.png', 'TITLE': 'Will Mt Gox’s First BTC Movement in 8 Months Add to Bitcoin’s Selling Pressure?', 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': 'Mandy Williams', 'URL': 'https://cryptopotato.com/will-mt-goxs-first-btc-movement-in-8-months-add-to-bitcoins-selling-pressure/', 'SOURCE_ID': 27, 'BODY': 'Bitcoin (BTC) has been under a lot of pressure recently, with its price dropping to levels not seen since mid-April 2025. Amid the persistent negative trend, one of the largest holders of BTC had executed a major transfer that is capable of shaking the market further. According to a tweet by Lookonchain, the estate trustee of the defunct cryptocurrency exchange Mt. Gox has moved approximately $1 billion in BTC within the last 24 hours. With the market already bleeding , the latest Mt. Gox transfer raises the question of whether BTC will buckle under intensifying selling pressure and decline further. Mt Gox Makes Bitcoin Moves The last time Mt Gox made a significant transfer was eight months ago, on March 25. CryptoPotato reported at the time that the entity moved 11,501 BTC, worth over $1.01 billion, from its cold wallet to two addresses. Following that transaction were two others worth more than $77 million each. Since then, the cold wallet holding the defunct estate’s bitcoins has remained nearly dormant, only executing transactions worth less than $300 at a go. About seven hours before press time, the wallet suddenly moved 10,608 BTC worth no less than $953.66 million. A subsequent transaction from the wallet moved $16.8 million worth of bitcoins to another address. In total, Mt. Gox has moved 10,793 BTC, worth $970.46 million, to two different addresses. The cold wallet still held $3.16 billion in BTC at press time. Based on historical data, large Mt. Gox transfers have consistently preceded significant sell-offs. This is because the defunct exchange’s creditors tend to offload their assets soon after repayments are made. Over a decade after its collapse, Mt. Gox began repaying creditors in July 2024. Although the payments were scheduled to be concluded last month, the entity announced that it was moving the deadline to October 2026. The estate trustee cited incomplete procedures as a reason for the change in plans. This means the Bitcoin market will witness more large transfers from wallets tied to the defunct entity in the coming months. Will BTC Dump Further? Mt. Gox may only be conducting some internal shuffling arrangements for the ongoing repayments, rather than immediately dumping the assets. However, past data shows that nearly every large transfer from the entity has led to a significant plunge in bitcoin’s price. Data from CoinMarketCap shows that BTC has tumbled over 6.6% from $95,000 to $89,300. Although the asset had rebounded to $91,000 at the time of writing, Bitcoin moves from wallets tied to Mt Gox could trigger a deeper correction. The post Will Mt Gox’s First BTC Movement in 8 Months Add to Bitcoin’s Selling Pressure? appeared first on CryptoPotato .', 'KEYWORDS': 'AA News|Crypto News|Bitcoin (BTC) Price|Mt. Gox', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'NEGATIVE', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1763476535, 'UPDATED_ON': None, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 27, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'cryptopotato', 'NAME': 'Crypto Potato', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://images.cryptocompare.com/news/default/cryptopotato.png', 'URL': 'https://cryptopotato.com/category/crypto-news/feed/', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': 1458086400, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 57, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1763476830, 'CREATED_ON': 1657730129, 'UPDATED_ON': 1711621041}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 14, 'NAME': 'BTC', 'CATEGORY': 'BTC'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 25, 'NAME': 'EXCHANGE', 'CATEGORY': 'EXCHANGE'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 37, 'NAME': 'MARKET', 'CATEGORY': 'MARKET'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 50, 'NAME': 'TRADING', 'CATEGORY': 'TRADING'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 211, 'NAME': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY', 'CATEGORY': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 54570432, 'GUID': 'https://bitcoinworld.co.in/?p=220336', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1763469635, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/82/default.png', 'TITLE': 'Spot SOL ETF Explosion: Fidelity and Canary Capital Launch Game-Changing Investment on July 18', 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': 'Editorial Team', 'URL': 'https://bitcoinworld.co.in/fidelity-canary-spot-sol-etf/', 'SOURCE_ID': 82, 'BODY': 'BitcoinWorld Spot SOL ETF Explosion: Fidelity and Canary Capital Launch Game-Changing Investment on July 18 Get ready for a groundbreaking moment in crypto investing! The highly anticipated spot SOL ETF from financial giants Fidelity and Canary Capital is confirmed to launch on July 18, according to Unfolded reports. This revolutionary product marks a significant milestone for Solana adoption and provides mainstream investors with unprecedented access to the popular blockchain network. What Makes This Spot SOL ETF So Revolutionary? The spot SOL ETF represents a major leap forward for cryptocurrency accessibility. Unlike futures-based products, this spot ETF will hold actual Solana tokens, giving investors direct exposure to SOL’s price movements. This approach eliminates the complexities of managing private keys while providing institutional-grade security through Fidelity’s established infrastructure. Traditional investors have been waiting for such opportunities to enter the crypto space safely. The spot SOL ETF bridges this gap perfectly by combining blockchain innovation with familiar investment structures. Moreover, it signals growing institutional confidence in Solana’s long-term viability as a leading blockchain platform. Why Should Investors Care About This Launch? The July 18 launch date creates multiple advantages for both new and experienced investors. Here are the key benefits: Regulatory Compliance : All necessary approvals are secured, ensuring full regulatory compliance Simplified Access : No technical knowledge required to invest in Solana Enhanced Security : Fidelity’s robust custody solutions protect your investment Tax Efficiency : ETF structure provides clear tax reporting advantages Liquidity Access : Trade easily through traditional brokerage accounts This spot SOL ETF particularly benefits retirement account holders who can now include Solana exposure in their IRAs and 401(k)s. The timing coincides with increasing institutional interest in alternative assets, making it perfectly positioned for current market trends. How Will This Impact the Broader Crypto Market? The introduction of this spot SOL ETF could trigger significant market movements across the cryptocurrency ecosystem. Historical patterns show that major ETF launches often correlate with increased mainstream adoption and price appreciation for the underlying asset. The Solana network might experience heightened developer activity and project launches as institutional money flows in. Other blockchain projects will likely watch this development closely, as successful implementation could pave the way for similar products. The spot SOL ETF success might encourage regulators to approve more cryptocurrency investment vehicles, potentially accelerating overall market maturation. What Challenges Might Investors Face? While the spot SOL ETF offers numerous advantages, investors should remain aware of potential challenges. Cryptocurrency markets remain volatile, and SOL price fluctuations could impact ETF performance. Regulatory changes could affect the product’s operations, though Fidelity’s 